WEBVTT

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:06.490
<i>Asu no egao no tame ni!
For the smiles of tomorrow!</i>

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.680
<i>Chikara to chikara butsukareba,
When power collides with power,</i>

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.270
<i>arasoi wa hajimaru.
wars start.</i>

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.820
<i>Tatakau koto ga</i> yuuki <i>to</i>
I <i>don't think fighting</i>

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.820
<i>omowanai kedo...
equals bravery, but...</i>

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.220
<i>...mamoritai yo
...I want to protect</i>

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.780
kimi <i>no sono egao.
that smile on your face.</i>

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.400
<i>Asu e no geeto
We can't see the gate</i>

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.090
<i>mienai keredo...
to tomorrow, but...</i>

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.870
<i>dare ni</i> demo <i>aru yo.
one's inside each of us.</i>

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.530
<i>Let's open the gate!</i>

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:49.240
Kinou <i>no namida</i> wa
<i>The tears we shed yesterday</i>

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.510
<i>kitto muda ja nai.
are probably not in vain.</i>

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:55.880
<i>Arasoi no nai</i> mirai wa
<i>A future without war</i>

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.650
<i>ano tobira no mukougawa.
waits behind that door.</i>

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.790
Mune <i>no oku</i> fukaku
<i>Retrieve the key lying</i>

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:06.730
<i>Jitto shimaikonda
deep inside your heart,</i>

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.530
<i>kagi wo takaku kakagete,
hold it up high,</i>

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:11.770
<i>fumidasou!
and step out!</i>

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:16.070
<i>Asu no egao no tame ni!
For the smiles of tomorrow!</i>

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:22.600
<i>You can open the gate!</i>

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:39.120
Low, low prices, everyone!
Herring roe for New Year's feast...

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:43.060
...is only 1,000 yen a box!
That's 1,000 yen!

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:46.070
You, ladies and daddies over there!
The Japanese New Year won't take off...

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:49.330
...without a Shinto straw decoration
and Kadomatsu pine decoration!

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.780
What's wrong?

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:01.680
Shun says he can't
come home for New Year's.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.080
What?!

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:05.680
He has many important
things to keep him busy.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.890
That's ridiculous! Nothing's more
important than coming home for New Year's!!

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:14.860
Nothing's more important.

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:16.900
Hey! you're Ukiya!

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.420
Ew, it's Takeshi!

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.030
What do you mean by "ew"?

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.600
Ukki-kki, Ukiya the chimpanzee!

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.240
Now you've done it!

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.950
Ukiya's punch is a monkey punch!
Ukiya's head is a monkey head!

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:37.920
<i>STOP !</i>

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.940
Ukiya...

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:49.620
The boarding lady said
that he's at school, but...

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.760
...there's no one here.

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:58.400
Big brother?

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:07.640
It's so high!

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.340
The desks are huge, too!

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:15.420
Join Track & Field Now!!

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.650
Club activities!
That looks like fun!

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:25.420
High school is great"!

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.190
Big brother, where are you?

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.290
Here, come here.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.630
You're so cute!

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:12.370
High school is great"!

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.710
Hisame...

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.710
Oh, good afternoon.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.640
Come, Hisame.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:25.780
So, he's called Hisame!
He tickles!

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:30.650
This is a weasel, isn't it?
I've never heard of a white weasel. He's cool!

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.950
Ermine.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:35.830
Ermine?

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:46.670
Are you telling me to follow?

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.210
You are, aren't you?!

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.650
Oh, wait!

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.550
Wait!

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.290
PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:05.660
Invaders do not observe
New Year's Eve or any other holiday.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:09.250
Therefore, to always be on alert
to deal with invader threat...

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:13.430
...l have asked that
you remain at school, but...

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:21.210
Over there...

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.940
Big brother?!!

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.740
Big brother?!!
Saemi?! What are you doing here?!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:34.580
Why aren't you coming home?!
School is off for the winter, isn't it?!

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:39.590
I'd like to, but I have to guard...
I mean, I have a research paper to do...

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:43.320
It's New Year's! You know,
Japan's most celebrated holiday...

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:46.890
...where everyone wishes
everyone else a happy new year?!

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:51.600
And you say you can't come home for one day?!
You stupid, stupid, stupid!

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.610
I'm sorry. Really.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.840
Mom looked forward to it, you know.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:02.510
She wanted to watch tomorrow's New Year's
Celebrity Singing Battle with you.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:15.350
I'm sorry, Saemi. I'm the one
who kept him from going.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:20.830
It's okay. Your big brother
will go home with you.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:24.430
Commander!

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:27.740
The principal's name is
"Mr. Koh Manda.”

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:29.440
That's right!

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:33.780
When you say your principal's name,
call him MISTER, big brother!

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:35.840
Right...

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:40.880
I'm Saemi Ukiya. I'm10.
Thank you for always putting up with my big brother.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:49.190
It's great that we all
get to go home now, huh?

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:53.470
Yeah, but both my parents
are in Hawaii. What will I do?

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.830
I also told my folks
I wouldn't be home for New Year's...

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:58.070
...so they're all out
visiting relatives in the country.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.800
Okay, so why don't all
of you come to our house?

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:01.570
What?!

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:04.130
Hey, that's a great idea!

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:07.110
New Year's at Ukiya's house...

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:12.540
I'll help prepare the New Year's feast!

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:14.780
But you're a guest.
You really don't have to...

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:18.160
A guest? Don't be such a stranger!

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:21.960
I sure am looking forward to having
your mother teach me how to cook!

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:33.840
I would love for eternity without
change of heart, but for how long?

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:38.870
Rather I die while my love be true.

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:41.650
Say!

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:43.840
What are you doing?
We're going now.

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.110
Going?

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:47.450
To my house! C'mon!

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:07.260
Brr... It's lonely in an empty dorm...
but it's actually more lonely in a hangar!

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:09.870
A real man doesn't whine and bellyache!

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:14.910
Yeah, but I came because you said we
would see the girls in their kimonos!

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:18.510
Since we did Christmas together, I thought
we'd be doing New Year's together as well...

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:21.750
I made a horrible error in judgment!!

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:33.890
This is the lkusawa's little Ruri. She's
grown into a fine young lady, don't you think?

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:36.060
Oh, please, Auntie Kazuko!

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:38.900
Well, I have to get the feast ready.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.770
I'll help.

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:46.550
I'll help, too, Mother!

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:53.850
You're doing great, Hisame!
Amazing! You're amazing!

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:57.220
Whoa! Look at him go!

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:06.020
This is wonderful! I haven't had
a house this lively in years!

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.500
I'll have to make lots of goodies!

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:10.160
<i>Yes, ma'am!</i>

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.940
Yukino doesn't say much, does she?

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:18.670
She was like that when Ukiya and I
first met her in the mountains, too.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.570
In the mountainsm?

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:25.520
Uh, no! I mean, when it happened,
it was kind of dreamy...

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:29.080
Dreamy...?

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.280
<i>What happened
between her and Ukiya?!</i>

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:42.060
You're very good at that, Kaoru.
I'm sure you'll be a wonderful wife.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:44.300
Thank you, Mother!

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.170
Good boy, good boy.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.340
You're lucky, Yukino.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:55.340
You have a pet. And not a cat or
a dog, but an ermine! You're trendy!

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:58.350
Trendy?

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:01.380
Yeah! You're ahead of the crowd!

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:03.860
Ahead of the crowd...?

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:30.680
This picture was taken on
my class field trip in the fall.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:34.880
It was my first time riding the
rope way, but the fog was so thick...

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.120
...l thought I wouldn't
be able to see anything.

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:41.630
Then, the wind suddenly blew really hard
and the rope way swung back and forth...

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:44.100
...and the weather turned great!

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:49.130
After that, way on the other side of the
clear blue sky I was able to see Mt. Fuji!

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:51.700
Yukino, have you ever seen Mt. Fuji?

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:55.900
Smoke from Mt. Fuji,
it vanishes in the sky.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:59.880
Like smoke, my love also
vanishes without a trace.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:02.780
What's that?

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:05.720
A song... of .. Mt. Fuji.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:09.580
That's an interesting song.
The song I know goes like this:

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:13.090
His head up above the clouds...

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:17.290
...he looks down all
mountains around him.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:21.060
He sees thunder way below.

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:26.010
Fuji is the best mountain
in Japan. Like that.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:36.180
Whew.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.050
Who is this?

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:48.100
A really nasty guy.
His name is Takeshi lkeda.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:52.100
He's the leader of the soccer team
and he thinks he's such hot stuff...

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:55.660
...but he's no good at schoolwork,
and he's mean, and he's violent...

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:57.700
...and he's a complete nitwit!

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:07.050
Oh, this is a picture from
last year's athletic festival!

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:10.450
I was in second place,
sol got a pencil.

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:13.680
If I had gotten first place,
I would have won a notebook.

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:17.850
This is the folkdance we held at the
school party for the upper graders.

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:25.760
And in this one, that idiot Takeshi
said he'd never hold hands with a girl...

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:31.100
...what an idiot. Yeesh. He doesn't
have the slightest idea how I...

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:33.830
Idiot.

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:02.270
Hello, may we come in?

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:05.060
Good afternoon!

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:08.300
Hello, I'm a rice cake dealer!

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:10.810
<i>- Reiko?
- Fei!</i>

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:13.780
I'm amazed you found my house!

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:17.480
The commander... I mean,
the principal told us how to get here.

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:21.040
Um, this is a small present.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:27.080
Me and Reiko just got off work from
our part-time jobs at the rice cake dealer.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:28.590
Part time jobs?!

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:31.830
That's right. It was for social studies!

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:35.560
Yeah, but we got fired in only
21 minutes and 15 seconds.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:39.230
They gave us this
as a farewell present.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:44.440
The owner of the shop
is a really nice man...

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:48.470
He cried and begged us
to please go home.

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.480
I see.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.120
Who's that?

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:56.160
Don't worry, I'll get it.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:59.490
Who is it...?

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:09.230
U- Uh...

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.270
Wh- What do you want?

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:17.840
Here.

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:26.820
I don't want this stupid thing!!

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:32.260
Ukiya...!

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:11.660
And after that, Reiko jumped
headfirst into pound rice cake!

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:14.170
Come on, Yukino.
There are showers over here!

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:17.600
Showers?
It was really hot...

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:24.440
But the most incredible part was when you
chased after the owner with the pounder.

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:25.980
What? She did?

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:29.050
Doesn't this feel great, Yukino?

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:30.350
lt's hot...
That pounder was really heavy! I could
do nothing but wobble, wobble, wobble...

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:34.310
Hey, you're right. You're bright red.

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:37.380
You look like a little baby!
Reiko, you're too funny!

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:40.960
Come over here. This tub has lukewarm water in it.
Come on!
Let's all wash each other's backs!

00:16:41.030 --> 00:16:41.960
Agreed!

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.420
Let' s go Yukino!.

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:46.930
Japanese baths are
big and comfortable.

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:48.470
Geronimo!

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:49.200
Japanese baths are
big and comfortable.

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:52.440
C'mon! You, too, Yukino!

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.440
Honestly... what am I to do with you two?

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:58.500
Now that I think about it,
tomorrow morning, New Year's Day...

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:02.670
...is my 18th birthday...!

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:03.450
Reiko, you're too funny!

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:04.950
It's hot...

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:05.920
R- Reiko, you're too funny!

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.550
It's so... so lonely...!

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:18.560
I bet Takeshi came to apologize.

00:17:20.070 --> 00:17:22.060
But I went and...

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:25.700
...l'm a horrible girl.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:35.110
The truth is, I like Takeshi.

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:38.520
But it's all over now.

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:45.850
I would love for eternity without
change of heart, but for how long?

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:49.020
Rather I die while my love be true.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:53.960
You always say complicated
things, don't you?

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.840
While my love be true...

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:05.310
Still, you're trying to cheer
me up, aren't you, Yukino!

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:13.750
Yukino,what is this?

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:16.350
It looks very good on you.

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:27.190
Huh?

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:31.840
The 20th Annual
Celebrity Song Battle

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:42.010
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, we have only
a few hours left to the New Year'!</i>

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:44.310
Thanks, Mr. Matsuda!!

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:47.750
<i>Mankind landed 0n the moon thls year'!
And we 'll celebrate...</i>
Don't <i>mention it. Your father always helped me out.</i>

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:50.760
to encourage the continued
progress and harmony of man!
You can use it for a while.

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:52.420
This is amazing...

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:55.860
Do you think someday all TV's
across Japan will be in color?!

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:57.490
That would be great!

00:18:57.560 --> 00:19:01.900
I wonder who paints
the colors on color TV?

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:04.770
It's a mystery, really...

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:05.760
Do you know?

00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:09.670
Oh, please!
How could I possibly know?

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:13.740
I would love for eternity without
change of heart, but for how long?

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:16.780
Rather I die while my love is true.

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:20.250
It's here!

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:24.080
You're late... uh...?

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:27.490
You're...

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:29.050
Takeshi!

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:39.140
Takeshi...!

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:41.170
I'm sorry!

00:19:45.610 --> 00:19:47.240
You're wearing it...

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:52.650
It was a waste to throw it away,
so l decided to keep it!

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:57.250
Throw it away?! I paid a lot
of my allowance for that!

00:19:57.560 --> 00:19:59.580
In your eye!

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:00.820
Why, you!

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:03.760
Takeshi, Takeshi,
tuckie sheets betwetter!

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:07.070
Saemi, enough of that.

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:12.260
You come in, too, Takeshi.
The song battle has begun.

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:16.010
Come to think of it, who
were you expecting, Ukiya?

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:20.010
That goes without saying!
For the buckwheat noodle delivery guy!

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:29.180
Let's go!

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:30.750
Right!

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:41.870
It sure is great your family
runs a ramen shop, Kurogane!

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:45.340
Okay, let's crash this party!

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:52.980
Enjoy it while you can.

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:29.640
That was a long prayer.
What did you wish for?

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:31.280
For brief life...

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:32.750
Huh?

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:37.350
I wished to be able live my life to
the fullest, because life is short.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:45.690
Line up together with everyone.

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:47.730
Okay, say cheese!

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.870
<i>The poetry written for a new year...</i>

00:21:52.940 --> 00:21:57.810
<i>...is a blessing for 1,000 years
of joy and happiness.</i>

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:11.230
<i>Itsumademo wasurenai
We received many things</i>

00:22:11.230 --> 00:22:15.100
<i>takusan no mono moratta ne.
we will never forget.</i>

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:20.070
<i>Sora no iro utsushite hikaru
I don't mean the blue jewels flashing</i>

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:23.440
<i>aoi houseki ya
with colors of the sky...</i>

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:25.580
koinu-tachi
or a big yard

00:22:25.580 --> 00:22:30.750
<i>hanemawaru hiroi</i> niwaja <i>nai,
with puppies romping around,</i>

00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:34.090
motto motto daijina
but something <i>much</i> more

00:22:34.090 --> 00:22:38.720
<i>mono wo.
important.</i>

00:22:39.430 --> 00:22:43.590
<i>Kinou Kara kyou e
From yesterday to today,</i>

00:22:43.660 --> 00:22:48.230
<i>kyou kara asu e to
from today to tomorrow,</i>

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:55.010
boku-tachi wa aruite yuku yo.
we will walk toward the future.
